# A parameter row shadowed by a same-named function (GH #266).
#
# This is the SBML `<assignmentRule>` shape after conversion to `.net`: the
# parameter keeps the species' *initial* value and the rule becomes a function
# of the same name. bngsim binds the function to the declared slot and
# `evaluate_functions()` overwrites it before every derivative evaluation — so
# the number in the `parameters` block is the seed that slot holds until the
# function first evaluates, and never a knob. `set_param` on it used to be
# accepted and discarded one step later.
#
# Tracked deliberately. The shape occurs in four models under
# `benchmarks/suites/ssa_table5/results/converted/` (BIOMD0000000344 alone leaks
# 83 names) and in **zero** of the 140 `.net` files tracked in git, so the sweep
# in `test_primary_param_names.py` was green in CI and red only on a machine
# that had generated that corpus. Without this file the fix has no CI coverage.
#
# Two shadowed rows, because the loader reaches them by different routes:
#   supply   0.0    a literal, so the `.net` reader flags it a plain constant —
#                   the case #227 left behind, and the one the four models have.
#   recycle  1/4    arithmetic, so the reader guesses `is_expression` from the
#                   value text. The slot is not *derived* either (nothing
#                   recomputes it from primaries; the function overwrites it),
#                   so the derived flag comes off and `is_internal` carries the
#                   fact — the two flags have to stay disjoint.
#
# Both are live: `supply` is the rate of a zero-order source, so a run that used
# the 0.0 seed instead of the function would leave A at zero forever.
begin parameters
    1 kdeg    0.20
    2 kmax    3.0
    3 supply  0.0
    4 recycle 1/4
end parameters
begin species
    1 A() 0
    2 B() 5
end species
begin reactions
    1 0 1 supply
    2 1 2 kdeg
    3 2 1 recycle
end reactions
begin groups
    1 A_obs 1
    2 B_obs 2
end groups
begin functions
    1 supply() kmax*B_obs/(1+B_obs)
    2 recycle() kdeg
end functions
